    {
      "body": "CI is currently blocked on the missing `run-ci` label — `pr-gate` fails\nimmediately and every test job skips, so nothing in this PR has actually been\nexercised yet. The 16 red checks are all that one gate, not test failures.\n\nCould a maintainer add the label (or run `/tag-run-ci-label`)? `lint` is green,\nand the change is rebased on current `main`. Happy to rebase again if anything\nmoves in the meantime.\n",
      "created_at": "2026-09-01T23:05:52Z",
      "html_url": "https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/pull/37470#issuecomment-5501650749",
      "id": 5501650749,
      "updated_at": "2026-09-01T23:05:52Z",
      "user": {
        "login": "vaibhavhariram"
      }
    },
    {
      "body": "I have restated #27255 against current main and verified the shared request-slicing path, including `background`, `use_audio_in_video`, `routing_key`, and the already-forwarded `require_reasoning`. The complete `test_io_struct.py` run has 67 passed, 2 skipped, and 16 subtests passed.\n\nI am using #27255 as the single lane for this fix. If you agree that it covers your PR's scope, please close this one so maintainers do not have to compare duplicate patches.\n",
